  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1206 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nMainly quiet weather will continue across South Texas this week. A\nweak disturbance over the western Gulf will bring a chance for\nshowers, and possibly a thunderstorm, tonight over the coast and \ncoastal waters. This feature will move inland to the southwest\nThursday with a low chance for showers across the southern portion\nof the CWA. A mid to upper level ridge will build over the region\nduring the end of the week keeping the weather dry through the\nweekend. Temperatures will continue to be just a bit above normal\nwith highs in the 80s. Low temperatures Thursday morning will be \na few degrees warmer than the last couple of days with more \ncloudiness from the westward moving disturbance. Clearer skies \nwill allow for cooler mornings over the weekend. Another weak \ndisturbance from the Gulf will bring a chance for rain next Monday\nwith better chances over the Coastal Plains. Tuesday models are \nshowing a frontal boundary moving through North Texas with an \nexpansive area of rain across the eastern half of the state. Still\na lot of uncertainty.\n\nGuidance continues to show elevated tidal levels and the potential \nfor minor coastal flooding continues through the week.",
